( --- SHARED CONTROL STATE + MEMORY HELPERS ---
  Was the "system memory map": a block of hand-picked addresses in the gap
  between the framebuffer and user memory. The addresses are gone -- state
  here is compiler-allocated now -- so what remains is the shared control
  cells and the byte-move helpers. )

MODULE MEMORY

( --- Controls System State ---
  The six cells lib/core.lux's x@/y@/w@/h@/base@/temp@ accessors sit on,
  also used directly by lib/draw.lux's string blitter. Compiler-allocated
  (docs/reserve-directive.md).

  Everything else that used to live here -- 24 constants for a dialog and
  file-dialog system (DIALOG_*, FILE_DIALOG_*, FP_*, FILE_DIR_*) spanning
  0x521000-0x533600 -- was dead: nothing in lib/ or apps/ referenced any of
  them, and none appear in abi/uisf.exports.json. They were dropped rather
  than reserved, since reserving ~78KB of buffers no code reads would spend
  most of the reservation band on nothing. lib/dialog.lux is the modal
  dialog implementation that is actually live. )
RESERVE CTRL_X    4 ;
RESERVE CTRL_Y    4 ;
RESERVE CTRL_W    4 ;
RESERVE CTRL_H    4 ;
RESERVE CTRL_BASE 4 ;
RESERVE CTRL_TEMP 4 ;

( --- Memory Manipulation --- )

@move-mem ( src dest len -- )
    3 frame!
    2 local@ 1 local@ < [
        ( Backward copy: src < dest, copy from high to low to avoid clobber )
        2 local@ 0 local@ + 1 -
        1 local@ 0 local@ + 1 -
        [ 0 local@ 0 > ] [
            OVER load-byte OVER store-byte
            1 - swap 1 - swap
            0 local@ 1 - 0 local!
        ] |:
        drop drop
    ] [
        ( Forward copy )
        [ 0 local@ 0 > ] [
            2 local@ load-byte 1 local@ store-byte
            2 local@ 1 + 2 local!
            1 local@ 1 + 1 local!
            0 local@ 1 - 0 local!
        ] |:
    ] ?:
    3 unframe!
;
